The code in this package (every .py file) is released under the MIT License below, except the five files in
figures/vendor/, which keep the Apache License 2.0 of their source (figures/vendor/LICENSE and figures/vendor/SOURCE.md).
The materials, the results and every other file are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The American Time Use Survey files, the Census occupation code
lists and the BLS occupation crosswalk are public files of the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics and the U.S. Census
Bureau; the package holds only their URLs and checksums (data/atus/MANIFEST.csv). The two files in analysis/reference/
are World Bank data (World Development Indicators, PA.NUS.PPP and PA.NUS.FCRF), released by the World Bank under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. The occupation scores of exposure to
generative AI in data/atus/derived/ are computed from the published files of Eloundou, Manning, Mishkin and Rock (2024)
and of Felten, Raj and Seamans (2021, 2023), and they keep the terms of those sources.

